  "result": "`Parameter.consume_value` (`core.py:2481`) returns a `(value, source)` tuple. It tries each source in turn and stops at the first one that supplies a value. A sentinel, `UNSET`, marks \"nothing found yet\".\n\n1. **Command line.** It reads `opts.get(self.name, UNSET)`, which is what the parser produced. If a value is there, the source is `ParameterSource.COMMANDLINE`. Otherwise the source starts as `DEFAULT`.\n2. **Environment variable.** If the value is still `UNSET`, it calls `value_from_envvar(ctx)`. A non-`None` result becomes the value, with source `ENVIRONMENT`.\n3. **`default_map`.** If the value is still `UNSET`, it calls `ctx.lookup_default(self.name)`. The result is used if it is non-`None`, or if the key is present in the map at all (`_default_map_has`), so an explicit `None` counts. The source is `DEFAULT_MAP`. A string value for a parameter with `nargs != 1` is split with `type.split_envvar_value`.\n4. **Parameter default.** If the value is still `UNSET`, it calls `get_default(ctx)`. A result other than `UNSET` is used, with source `DEFAULT`.\n\nIf nothing matches, it returns `UNSET` with source `DEFAULT`.\n\n`Option.consume_value` (`core.py:3589`) wraps this. If the parser returned the `FLAG_NEEDS_VALUE` sentinel, it uses the prompt (source `PROMPT`) when a prompt is configured. Otherwise it uses the flag's activation value (source `COMMANDLINE`).",
